  "tagline": "Multi-model Java database speaking SQL, Cypher, Gremlin, MongoDB and Redis protocols.",
  "description": "ArcadeDB is an open-source multi-model database by Luca Garulli, the creator of OrientDB, and is a conceptual successor to it rebuilt for lower overhead. A single engine stores graphs, documents, key-value pairs, time series and vector embeddings, and you can query it with its SQL dialect, openCypher, Gremlin or GraphQL, or connect over the PostgreSQL, MongoDB and Redis wire protocols. It runs embedded in a JVM or as a server with Raft-based replication. It is a good fit when you want one flexible, Apache-licensed store for mixed graph and document data, but it is a small project with modest community adoption.",
